<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sasol says to export excess fuel alcohol.</title>
<headline>Sasol says to export excess fuel alcohol.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sasol Ltd said it had developed alternative export markets for fuel alcohol produced by the company and as a result alcohol will not be re-introduced into South African petrol on September 1, as previously planned.  </p>
<p>Export prospects for synthetic fuel alcohol appeared promising but Sasol said this outlet could not be guaranteed, so it might be necessary to re-introduce alcohol into the South African petrol pool at a later date.</p>
<p>If this should happen, Sasol would comply with fuel specifications allowing for up to 12 percent alcohol in inland petrol, the company added.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
